5.5 Bar Stock Consumption
The barman should not manually calculate stock consumption.
When a bono is redeemed or a paid drink is sold, the system should automatically deduct the configured stock quantity.
For example:
1 bottle of soft drink = 1 unit.
1 glass of juice = configured quantity of juice ingredients.
1 bottle of beer = 1 unit.
1 cocktail = configured quantities of multiple ingredients.
This requires a product recipe or Bill of Materials (BOM) functionality for products prepared from multiple ingredients.
The system should also track stock adjustments, wastage, damaged products, and complimentary consumption.
