18.1 Critical Bono Accounting Consideration
A bono may represent a financial obligation even before it is redeemed.
Therefore, the system should distinguish:
Bono issued.
Bono outstanding.
Bono redeemed.
Bono expired.
Bono cancelled.
The hotel should configure whether bonos are prepaid, complimentary, promotional, or employee-authorized.
This prevents management from confusing the number of drinks served with actual cash revenue.
18.2 Critical Inventory Consideration
The system should differentiate between:
Stock received by the main store.
Stock transferred to the bar.
Stock transferred to the kitchen.
Stock sold to customers.
Stock consumed through bonos.
Stock used for preparation.
Stock damaged or wasted.
This is necessary to make stock reconciliation accurate.
