The ultimate goal: One Platform. Complete Operational Control. Measurable Business Performance.
23. My Strategic Recommendations for BelTech Solutions
I would make five design decisions before development starts:
1. Build it as a product, not a one-client application. Every hotel should have its own configurable departments, users, products, payment methods, and bono rules.
2. Make the POS exceptionally simple. Cashiers and barmen should be able to process transactions quickly without navigating complicated ERP screens.
3. Treat bono management as a core competitive feature. Many generic restaurant POS systems do not provide the level of voucher issuance, redemption, stock deduction, and reconciliation control described here.
4. Make inventory and finance fully integrated. Avoid separate records that require manual reconciliation.
5. Prioritize management reporting. Your dashboard and employee-level accountability can become major selling points when approaching hotels and restaurants.
